pass 11 security + drift detection. security: NEOHIRO_DEBUG_LOG is now created with mode 0600 (owner-only) via install -m 0600, so command arguments written to it by _log_error (e.g., passwords passed to run sudo -S ...) are not world-readable. Added SECURITY NOTE in lib/temp.sh header. robustness: lib/sync-inline.sh detects drift between the canonical lib files and the inline fallbacks in top-level scripts -- previously the inline was a manual copy-paste that could silently diverge from the lib (which is exactly what pass 9 caught for DeepClean.sh set -u and run() DRY_RUN on ubuntu). removed _clean_temp helper from lib/temp.sh in favor of the inline-equivalent trap string so both paths can be structurally verified.
